cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt these materials, please cite them as below."
title: "Understanding AI: A Practical Workshop for Humanities and Social Science Researchers"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pizzorno
    given-names: Gabriel H.
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpizzorno/understanding-ai"
url: "https://github.com/gpizzorno/understanding-ai"
abstract: >-
  Teaching materials introducing humanities and social science researchers to
  contemporary AI systems: key concepts, effective and critical use of large
  language models, and a Python case study using pre-trained named-entity
  recognition models on the letters of Robert Louis Stevenson. Designed for
  self-study and for in-person workshops.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - large language models
  - digital humanities
  - named-entity recognition
  - teaching materials
